  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Data exploration:** The data view `kibana_sample_data_logs` uses `timestamp` as its time field. The useful fields are `clientip`, `bytes`, `response` (with `response.keyword`), `url`, `request`, `geo.*`, `agent`, and `extension`.\n\n**Dashboard: `EFF-2a671d4f Web logs overview`**\n- ID: `eff-2a671d4f-web-logs-overview-12457f4b3487`\n- URL: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-2a671d4f-web-logs-overview-12457f4b3487\n- Five panels, default time range last 7 days:\n  - Total requests (count metric)\n  - Unique client IPs (unique count of `clientip`)\n  - Total bytes served (sum of `bytes`)\n  - Requests over time (line, date histogram on `timestamp`)\n  - Responses by status code (bar, terms on `response.keyword`)\n\n**Alert rule: `EFF-2a671d4f 5xx spike`**\n- ID: `c924504e-e34b-43fa-954b-5d9d0563f719`\n- Type `.es-query`, runs every 1m, enabled.\n- Condition: fires when the count of documents in the last 5 minutes is greater than 10.\n- 5xx filter: wildcard `response.keyword: \"5*\"`.\n- I added the tag `EFF-2a671d4f`. You didn't ask for it, so remove it if you don't want it.\n\n**Not verified:**\n- The `KIBANA_TEST_API_KEY` variable is empty in my shell, and direct API calls returned 401. I used the Kibana MCP tools, which are authenticated. So I couldn't inspect the actual response-code values in the index. I assumed 5xx codes are stored as three-digit strings, which the wildcard relies on.\n- The rule reports `pending` status. I didn't wait for its first run, so I haven't confirmed it evaluates without errors.",
